WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.858 --> 00:00:16.868
Aunt Julia and Uncle John ignored Oliver's screaming.

2
00:00:18.569 --> 00:00:23.352
I can tell you that it wasn't easy because he was screaming really loud.

3
00:00:23.452 --> 00:00:25.554
They just acted like everything was normal.

4
00:00:25.574 --> 00:00:31.114
"Well," said Aunt Julia, "our cruise ship leaves in two hours."

5
00:00:31.134 --> 00:00:32.916
"That's right.

6
00:00:33.236 --> 00:00:34.597
We don't want to miss the boat!"

7
00:00:35.037 --> 00:00:35.938
said Uncle John.

8
00:00:35.958 --> 00:00:38.000
"So long, Oliver.

9
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.761
You have our cell phone numbers!"

10
00:00:39.781 --> 00:00:42.744
"I'm not staying here!"

11
00:00:43.124 --> 00:00:43.905
yelled Oliver.

12
00:00:43.925 --> 00:00:50.350
"We'll be back before you know it," said Aunt Julia, giving Oliver a hug.

13
00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:53.973
"Don't forget to brush your teeth, sweetie."

14
00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:57.476
And then they were gone.

15
00:00:58.912 --> 00:01:02.033
"Hey, Oliver," I said, before he could start screaming again.

16
00:01:02.053 --> 00:01:06.314
"Want to see the bed we made for you on the floor?

17
00:01:06.754 --> 00:01:08.115
It's right next to mine."

18
00:01:10.915 --> 00:01:11.916
Oliver shook his head.

19
00:01:11.936 --> 00:01:14.556
"I want to go home!"

20
00:01:15.096 --> 00:01:15.877
he cried.

21
00:01:19.118 --> 00:01:20.658
Mom put her arm around him.

22
00:01:20.678 --> 00:01:25.619
"I'm sure you'll be very happy here, Oliver," she said.

23
00:01:25.639 --> 00:01:28.040
"We'll have lots of fun."

24
00:01:31.644 --> 00:01:34.026
Oliver opened his mouth to start yelling again.

25
00:01:34.046 --> 00:01:40.591
"I want—" "Let's play Princesses and Pirates!"

26
00:01:41.071 --> 00:01:42.072
interrupted Jenny.

27
00:01:43.593 --> 00:01:44.554
Oliver shut his mouth.

28
00:01:44.574 --> 00:01:49.298
"That's a stupid game," he said in a grumpy voice.

29
00:01:50.399 --> 00:01:55.563
Boy, if anyone needed an attitude adjustment, it was Oliver.

30
00:01:59.788 --> 00:02:01.530
"Would you like a hot dog, Oliver?"

31
00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:02.871
asked my mom.

32
00:02:03.952 --> 00:02:04.953
Oliver shook his head.

33
00:02:04.973 --> 00:02:10.157
"My mom says hot dogs are bad for you," he said.

34
00:02:10.177 --> 00:02:13.961
"She says you don't know what's really in them."

35
00:02:13.981 --> 00:02:15.983
"What's really in them?"

36
00:02:16.423 --> 00:02:16.903
I asked.

37
00:02:16.923 --> 00:02:21.908
"Slimy snake guts," said Oliver.

38
00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.232
Josh and I burst out laughing.

39
00:02:27.264 --> 00:02:29.906
Oliver seemed surprised that we thought that was funny.

40
00:02:35.011 --> 00:02:37.072
Oliver complained all through dinner.

41
00:02:40.155 --> 00:02:42.056
At bedtime I took him to my room.

42
00:02:43.317 --> 00:02:45.819
I showed him the bed we'd made on the floor.

43
00:02:45.839 --> 00:02:50.743
"And look, my room has a skylight," I said.

44
00:02:50.763 --> 00:02:53.125
"You can see the moon."

45
00:02:54.887 --> 00:02:56.308
I pointed to the skylight.

46
00:02:58.472 --> 00:03:01.094
But Oliver did not seem interested in the moon.

47
00:03:02.195 --> 00:03:05.297
Instead he took his toothbrush out of his suitcase.

48
00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:09.059
"You have to brush your teeth in the kitchen," I explained.

49
00:03:09.079 --> 00:03:12.041
"Why?" asked Oliver.

50
00:03:12.061 --> 00:03:15.764
"Because there's no sink in our bathroom," I said.

51
00:03:15.784 --> 00:03:18.306
"Who ever heard of that?"

52
00:03:18.766 --> 00:03:19.646
said Oliver.

53
00:03:21.228 --> 00:03:23.209
Our bathroom is kind of weird.

54
00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.472
First of all, it's right next to the kitchen.

55
00:03:28.552 --> 00:03:30.994
And because it's so small, there's no room for a sink.

56
00:03:32.856 --> 00:03:35.078
That's why you have to brush your teeth in the kitchen.

57
00:03:35.098 --> 00:03:44.425
"Boy, that's the smallest bathroom I ever saw," said Oliver when he came back to my room.

58
00:03:44.445 --> 00:03:48.649
"Our bathroom at home is as big as your whole kitchen."

59
00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:53.793
By now I was sick of listening to Oliver complain.

60
00:03:54.954 --> 00:03:56.796
I just wanted him to go to sleep!

61
00:03:58.596 --> 00:04:00.117
Oliver lay down on his bed.

62
00:04:01.058 --> 00:04:02.079
I turned out the light.

63
00:04:02.099 --> 00:04:07.663
"I've never slept on the floor before," he said.

64
00:04:08.784 --> 00:04:10.125
He didn't sound too happy.

65
00:04:11.586 --> 00:04:14.087
I closed my eyes and pretended to be asleep.

66
00:04:14.107 --> 00:04:18.571
"You gave me a frog pillow," said Oliver.

67
00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:21.513
"I hate frogs!"

68
00:04:22.694 --> 00:04:25.155
I started snoring very loudly.

69
00:04:26.272 --> 00:04:29.155
"I can't sleep with a frog pillow!"

70
00:04:29.755 --> 00:04:30.776
wailed Oliver.

71
00:04:30.796 --> 00:04:34.099
"I hate the color green!"

72
00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:39.623
He kept moaning and complaining.

73
00:04:42.686 --> 00:04:44.467
I tossed and turned in my bed.

74
00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:48.711
Finally I sat up.

75
00:04:48.731 --> 00:04:50.292
"I give up!"

76
00:04:50.813 --> 00:04:51.313
I shouted.

77
00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:53.235
"You can have my bed!

78
00:04:53.255 --> 00:04:54.476
I'll sleep on the floor!"

79
00:04:55.592 --> 00:04:58.213
To my surprise there was no answer from Oliver.

80
00:04:59.294 --> 00:05:00.615
I leaned over and looked at him.

81
00:05:01.735 --> 00:05:05.457
He was curled up on his bed in the moonlight, sound asleep.

82
00:05:05.477 --> 00:05:07.698
"Thank goodness!"

83
00:05:08.058 --> 00:05:08.559
I thought.

84
00:05:09.499 --> 00:05:12.341
As I lay back down, I realized something.

85
00:05:13.361 --> 00:05:14.182
Tate was right.

86
00:05:15.582 --> 00:05:18.264
Being a big brother was a lot harder than I had thought.
